; Cubase-compatible key bindings for DAWFLOW
; This file maps Cubase 15 Pro default keyboard shortcuts to Ardour actions.
;
; FORMAT:
; $text -> defines cheatsheet title as "text", which may contain LaTeX markup
;
; %group owner text -> defines a binding group
;
; @group|action|binding|description -> defines an action+binding with description
;
; <Primary> = Cmd on macOS / Ctrl on Linux+Windows
; <Secondary> = Alt/Option
; <Tertiary> = Shift

;; Title
$DAWFLOW Shortcuts \linebreak Cubase-Compatible Layout

;; GROUP DEFINITIONS

%trans Global Global Transport \& Recording Control

%sess Global Global Session \& File Handling

%edit Editor Basic Editing

%vis Editor Changing What's Visible

%vws Editor Editor Views

%numpad Global Global NumPad Transport Functions

%gedt Global Global Editing Operations

%wvis Global Global Window Visibility

%edtrk Editor Track Actions from the Editor

%eep Editor Editing with Edit Point

%aep Editor Aligning with the Edit Point
Align operations move regions so that their start/end/sync point is at the edit point.

%gmark Global Global Marker Operations

%gmode Global Global Transport Modes

%gmon Global Global Monitor Operations

%movp Global Global Playhead Operations

%emov Editor Moving the Playhead in the Editor

%rop Editor Region Operations

%grid Editing Grid Settings + Editor Modes

%select Editor Selecting

%gselect Global Selecting

%ranges Editor Defining Loop, Punch Range and Tempo Changes

%markers Editor Markers \& Locations

%mmode Editing Mouse Modes
%emmode Editor Mouse Modes

%mouse Editing Mouse Usage

%mobject Editor Mouse Object Mode

%mzoom Editor Mouse Zoom Mode
%mops Editor Mouse Ops on Solo/Mute/Rec-enable
%mopsolo Editor Mouse Ops on Solo Buttons only
%mopsfader Editor Mouse Ops on Faders \& Plugin Controls

%midi Global Global MIDI commands

%notes MIDI Note Editing
%editing Editing Shared Editing

%rec Recorder Recorder Page

;; END GROUP DEFINITIONS

;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;
;; CUBASE-COMPATIBLE SHORTCUTS
;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;

;; =============================================================
;; TRANSPORT (Cubase-style)
;; =============================================================

; Space = Start/Stop (same as Cubase)
@trans|Transport/ToggleRoll|                                            space|start/stop playback
@trans|Transport/PlaySelection|                            <@SECONDARY@>space|play selection range
@trans|Transport/ToggleRollMaybe|               <@PRIMARY@><@SECONDARY@>space|stop (keep loop/range play)
@trans|Transport/ToggleRollForgetCapture|                    <@PRIMARY@>space|stop and forget capture
@trans|Transport/record-roll|                               <@TERTIARY@>space|start recording

; Return/Enter = Go to project start (Cubase: Enter/Numpad Enter)
@movp|Transport/alternate-GotoStart|                                   Return|go to project start

; Record (Cubase: Numpad *)
@trans|Transport/Record|                                   <@TERTIARY@>r|engage record

; Cycle/Loop on-off (Cubase: Numpad / mapped to L for loop in Ardour since no direct numpad / action)
@trans|Transport/Loop|                                                 l|loop play (the loop range)

; Metronome (Cubase: C)
@gmode|Transport/ToggleClick|                                          c|toggle metronome click

; Auto-scroll on/off (Cubase: F)
@edit|EditorEditing/toggle-follow-playhead|                            f|auto-scroll on/off

; Rewind/Forward (Cubase: Shift+Left/Right mapped to Ardour)
@trans|Transport/Rewind|                                  <@TERTIARY@>Left|rewind
@trans|Transport/Forward|                                <@TERTIARY@>Right|fast forward
@trans|Transport/TransitionToRoll|                        <@TERTIARY@>Up|transition to roll
@trans|Transport/TransitionToReverse|                   <@TERTIARY@>Down|transition to reverse

; Punch In/Out (Cubase: I for Punch In, O for Punch Out)
; Note: Ardour has TogglePunch for both; we map 8 to keep Cubase number key convention nearby
@gmode|Transport/TogglePunch|                                          8|toggle punch in+out

; Auto Return (Cubase: 7 area)
@gmode|Transport/ToggleAutoReturn|                                     7|toggle auto return
@gmode|Transport/ToggleAutoPlay|                            <@PRIMARY@>7|toggle auto play

; Follow Edits
@gmode|Transport/ToggleFollowEdits|           <@PRIMARY@>3|toggle playhead follows edits

; External sync (Cubase: Alt+Shift+T)
@trans|Transport/ToggleExternalSync|    <@SECONDARY@><@TERTIARY@>t|toggle external sync


;; =============================================================
;; TOOL SELECTION (Cubase number key mapping)
;; =============================================================
;; Cubase:  1=Select, 2=Range, 3=Split, 4=Glue, 5=Erase, 6=Zoom, 7=Mute, 8=Draw, 9=Play
;; Ardour equivalents mapped below

; 1 = Object Selection Tool (Cubase: Select/Arrow tool)
@mmode|Editing/set-mouse-mode-object|                                  1|select tool (object)

; 2 = Range Selection Tool (Cubase: Range tool)
@mmode|Editing/set-mouse-mode-range|                                   2|range selection tool

; 3 = Split/Scissors Tool (Cubase: Split tool)
@mmode|Editing/set-mouse-mode-cut|                                     3|split tool (scissors)

; 4 = Glue Tool -> mapped to Content mode (closest Ardour equivalent)
@mmode|Editing/set-mouse-mode-content|                                 4|content tool (glue equivalent)

; 5 = Erase Tool -> no direct equivalent; use Draw mode as closest
@mmode|Editing/set-mouse-mode-draw|                                    5|draw tool (erase equivalent)

; 6 = Zoom Tool -> mapped to Grid mode (Ardour has zoom via G/H keys)
@mmode|Editing/set-mouse-mode-grid|                                    6|grid tool

; 7 = Mute Tool -> no direct mouse mode; available via M key for mute
; (reserved for auto return toggle above)

; 8 = Draw/Pencil Tool -> mapped to TimeFX mode
; (reserved for punch toggle above)

; 9 = Play Tool -> mapped to Ardour's set-tempo-from-region
@ranges|Region/set-tempo-from-region|                                  9|set tempo (1 bar) from region(s)

; 0 = Drumstick Tool -> no equivalent; use set-tempo-from-edit-range
@ranges|Editor/set-tempo-from-edit-range|                              0|set tempo (1 bar) from edit range

; Smart Mode (Cubase doesn't have this but Ardour does — keep on Shift+1)
@emmode|Editor/set-mouse-mode-object-range|         <@TERTIARY@>1|smart mode (object + range)


;; =============================================================
;; EDITING (Cubase-style)
;; =============================================================

; Undo/Redo (Cubase: Cmd+Z / Cmd+Shift+Z)
@editing|Editing/undo|                                       <@PRIMARY@>z|undo
@editing|Editing/alternate-alternate-redo|       <@PRIMARY@><@TERTIARY@>z|redo

; Cut/Copy/Paste (Cubase: Cmd+X/C/V — same as standard)
@editing|Editing/editor-cut|                                 <@PRIMARY@>x|cut
@editing|Editing/editor-copy|                                <@PRIMARY@>c|copy
@editing|Editing/editor-paste|                               <@PRIMARY@>v|paste

; Delete (Cubase: Delete/Backspace)
@editing|Editing/editor-delete|                                   Delete|delete
@editing|Editing/alternate-editor-delete|                      BackSpace|backspace (delete)

; Select All (Cubase: Cmd+A)
@select|Editor/select-all-objects|                          <@PRIMARY@>a|select all objects

; Select None (Cubase: Cmd+Shift+A)
; Note: Ardour doesn't have a direct "deselect all" action — Escape does this
@gedt|Main/Escape|Escape|deselect all

; Duplicate (Cubase: Cmd+D)
@edit|Editor/duplicate|                                     <@PRIMARY@>d|duplicate (once)

; Repeat/Multi-duplicate (Cubase: Cmd+K)
@edit|Editor/multi-duplicate|                               <@PRIMARY@>k|repeat / multi-duplicate

; Split at Cursor (Cubase: Alt+X)
@rop|Editor/split-region|                                  <@SECONDARY@>x|split at cursor

; Crossfade (Cubase: X)
@edit|Editor/editor-fade-range|                                        x|crossfade / fade range

; Mute events (Cubase: M)
@rop|Region/toggle-region-mute|                                        m|mute/unmute region

; Solo (Cubase: S)
@trans|Transport/solo-selection|                                        s|solo selection

; Record Enable (Cubase: R)
; (Shift+R already used for engage record above)

; Move to Cursor (Cubase: Cmd+L)
@edit|Editor/find-and-display-stripable|                    <@PRIMARY@>l|find and display track/bus

; Snap On/Off (Cubase: J)
@grid|Editing/cycle-snap-mode|                                         j|cycle snap mode on/off

; Quantize (Cubase: Q)
@gmark|Common/jump-backward-to-mark|                                  q|to previous mark

; Left Selection Side to Cursor (Cubase: E)
@mmode|Editing/set-mouse-mode-content|                                 e|content mode

; Right Selection Side to Cursor (Cubase: D)
; d is used for duplicate with Cmd

; Move to Front (Cubase: U)
@select|Editor/select-all-within-cursors|                              u|select all regions touched by range

; Locators to Selection (Cubase: P)
@edit|Editor/set-playhead|                                             p|set playhead position


;; =============================================================
;; ZOOM (Cubase-style: H=Zoom In, G=Zoom Out)
;; =============================================================

; Zoom In (Cubase: H)
@editing|Editing/temporal-zoom-in|                                     h|zoom in (horizontal)

; Zoom Out (Cubase: G)
@editing|Editing/temporal-zoom-out|                                    g|zoom out (horizontal)

; Zoom In Vertically (Cubase: Shift+H)
@vis|Editor/expand-tracks|                                <@TERTIARY@>h|expand track height (zoom in vertical)

; Zoom Out Vertically (Cubase: Shift+G)
@vis|Editor/shrink-tracks|                                <@TERTIARY@>g|shrink track height (zoom out vertical)

; Zoom Full / Fit Project (Cubase: Shift+F)
@vis|Editor/zoom-to-session|                              <@TERTIARY@>f|zoom to fit entire session

; Zoom to Selection (Cubase: Alt+S)
@emmode|Editor/zoom-to-selection|                         <@SECONDARY@>s|zoom to selection

; Toggle last 2 zoom states
@vis|Editor/toggle-zoom|                                  <@TERTIARY@>z|toggle last 2 zoom states

; Fit Selection vertically
@vis|Editor/fit-selection|                          <@SECONDARY@><@TERTIARY@>f|fit selection vertically

; Zoom In Tracks (Cubase: Cmd+Down — Ardour uses Secondary+equal)
; Zoom Out Tracks (Cubase: Cmd+Up)


;; =============================================================
;; NAVIGATION (Cubase-style)
;; =============================================================

; Left/Right arrows = navigate to grid points
@movp|Common/playhead-backward-to-grid|                              Left|to previous grid point
@movp|Common/playhead-forward-to-grid|                              Right|to next grid point

; Cmd+Left/Right = move to transient
@emov|Editor/tab-to-transient-backwards|                  <@PRIMARY@>Left|to previous transient
@emov|Editor/tab-to-transient-forwards|                  <@PRIMARY@>Right|to next transient

; Up/Down arrows = scroll tracks
@vis|Editor/step-tracks-up|                                           Up|scroll up (step)
@vis|Editor/step-tracks-down|                                       Down|scroll down (step)

; Alt+Up/Down = select prev/next track (Cubase: just Up/Down but we need those for scroll)
@select|Editor/select-prev-route|                        <@SECONDARY@>Up|select previous track/bus
@select|Editor/select-next-route|                      <@SECONDARY@>Down|select next track/bus

; Home/End = go to start/end
@movp|Transport/GotoStart|                                         Home|go to start
@movp|Transport/GotoEnd|                                            End|go to end

; Page Up/Down
@vis|Editor/scroll-tracks-down|               Page_Down|scroll down (page)
@vis|Editor/scroll-tracks-up|                   Page_Up|scroll up (page)

; Locate Next/Previous Event (Cubase: N / B)
@gmark|Common/jump-forward-to-mark|                                   n|to next marker
@gmark|Common/jump-backward-to-mark|                                  b|to previous marker (locate previous)

; Nudge
@movp|Common/nudge-playhead-backward|                    <@SECONDARY@>Left|nudge backward
@movp|Common/nudge-playhead-forward|                   <@SECONDARY@>Right|nudge forward

; Region edge navigation
@emov|Editor/playhead-to-previous-region-boundary|  <@SECONDARY@><@TERTIARY@>Left|to previous region edge
@emov|Editor/playhead-to-next-region-boundary|     <@SECONDARY@><@TERTIARY@>Right|to next region edge

; Marker movement
@markers|Editor/selected-marker-to-previous-region-boundary|<@PRIMARY@><@TERTIARY@>Left|move marker to prev region edge
@markers|Editor/selected-marker-to-next-region-boundary|   <@PRIMARY@><@TERTIARY@>Right|move marker to next region edge


;; =============================================================
;; MARKERS (Cubase-style)
;; =============================================================

; Add marker (Cubase: Insert on Windows, Tab in Ardour)
@gmark|Common/add-location-from-playhead|                           Tab|add marker at playhead
@gmark|Common/remove-location-from-playhead|              <@PRIMARY@>Tab|remove marker at playhead

; Locate Selection Start (Cubase: L)
; L is used for loop above, so we use Shift+L
@select|Editor/select-all-in-loop-range|                   <@PRIMARY@>l|select all in loop range


;; =============================================================
;; WINDOWS / VIEWS (Cubase-style)
;; =============================================================

; Mixer (Cubase: F3)
@wvis|Common/show-mixer|                                             F3|show mixer window

; Transport Panel (Cubase: F2)
; No direct equivalent panel toggle in Ardour, use visual state
@vws|Editor/goto-visual-state-2|                                     F2|goto visual state 2

; MediaBay (Cubase: F5 — map to Ardour's import)
@vws|Editor/goto-visual-state-5|                                     F5|goto visual state 5

; Automation Panel (Cubase: F6)
@vws|Editor/goto-visual-state-6|                                     F6|goto visual state 6

; Direct Offline Processing (Cubase: F7)
@vws|Editor/goto-visual-state-7|                                     F7|goto visual state 7

; Video (Cubase: F8)
@edit|Editor/ToggleJadeo|                                            F8|toggle video window

; VST Instruments (Cubase: F11)
@vws|Editor/goto-visual-state-11|                                   F11|goto visual state 11

; VST Performance (Cubase: F12)
@vws|Editor/goto-visual-state-12|                                   F12|goto visual state 12

; Save visual states with Cmd+F-keys
@vws|Editor/save-visual-state-1|<@PRIMARY@>F1|save visual state 1
@vws|Editor/save-visual-state-2|<@PRIMARY@>F2|save visual state 2
@vws|Editor/save-visual-state-3|<@PRIMARY@>F3|save visual state 3
@vws|Editor/save-visual-state-4|<@PRIMARY@>F4|save visual state 4
@vws|Editor/save-visual-state-5|<@PRIMARY@>F5|save visual state 5
@vws|Editor/save-visual-state-6|<@PRIMARY@>F6|save visual state 6
@vws|Editor/save-visual-state-7|<@PRIMARY@>F7|save visual state 7
@vws|Editor/save-visual-state-8|<@PRIMARY@>F8|save visual state 8
@vws|Editor/save-visual-state-9|<@PRIMARY@>F9|save visual state 9
@vws|Editor/save-visual-state-10|<@PRIMARY@>F10|save visual state 10
@vws|Editor/save-visual-state-11|<@PRIMARY@>F11|save visual state 11
@vws|Editor/save-visual-state-12|<@PRIMARY@>F12|save visual state 12

; Remaining visual state recall
@vws|Editor/goto-visual-state-1|F1|goto visual state 1
@vws|Editor/goto-visual-state-3|F3|goto visual state 3 (overridden by mixer)
@vws|Editor/goto-visual-state-4|F4|goto visual state 4
@vws|Editor/goto-visual-state-8|F8|goto visual state 8 (overridden by video)
@vws|Editor/goto-visual-state-9|F9|goto visual state 9
@vws|Editor/goto-visual-state-10|F10|goto visual state 10

; Other window toggles
@wvis|Common/show-editor|                                <@SECONDARY@>e|show editor window
@wvis|Common/show-recorder|                               <@SECONDARY@>r|show recorder page
@wvis|Common/show-trigger|                                <@SECONDARY@>d|show cues page
@wvis|Common/toggle-meterbridge|                          <@SECONDARY@>b|show meter bridge
@wvis|Window/toggle-session-options-editor|               <@SECONDARY@>o|toggle preferences
@wvis|Window/toggle-locations|                            <@SECONDARY@>l|toggle locations dialog
@wvis|Window/toggle-virtual-keyboard|                     <@SECONDARY@>k|virtual MIDI keyboard
@wvis|Common/ToggleMaximalEditor|              <@PRIMARY@><@SECONDARY@>f|maximise editor space
@wvis|Common/ToggleMaximalMixer|                <@PRIMARY@><@TERTIARY@>f|maximise mixer space
@wvis|Window/toggle-audio-connection-manager| <@SECONDARY@><@TERTIARY@>a|toggle audio patchbay
@wvis|Window/toggle-midi-connection-manager|  <@SECONDARY@><@TERTIARY@>m|toggle midi patchbay
@wvis|Common/next-tab|             <@PRIMARY@>Page_Down|next tab
@wvis|Common/previous-tab|           <@PRIMARY@>Page_Up|previous tab
@wvis|Transport/focus-on-clock|                                 KP_Divide|focus on main clock

; Editor toggles
@vis|Editor/show-editor-mixer|                             <@TERTIARY@>e|toggle editor window mixer
@vis|Editor/show-editor-props|                             <@TERTIARY@>p|toggle editor properties
@edit|Editor/ToggleSummary|                                <@TERTIARY@>s|toggle summary
@edit|Editor/show-editor-list|                             <@TERTIARY@>l|show editor list


;; =============================================================
;; SESSION / FILE (Cubase-style)
;; =============================================================

; File operations (same as standard macOS/Cubase)
@sess|Common/Quit|                                          <@PRIMARY@>q|quit
@sess|Common/Save|                                          <@PRIMARY@>s|save session
@sess|Main/New|                                             <@PRIMARY@>n|new session
@sess|Main/Open|                                            <@PRIMARY@>o|open session
@sess|Main/SnapshotStay|                        <@PRIMARY@><@TERTIARY@>s|save as / snapshot
@sess|Main/QuickExport|                                     <@PRIMARY@>e|quick export

; Export (Cubase: Cmd+Shift+M for Audio Mixdown — Ardour doesn't have that exact shortcut)
@sess|Main/ExportAudio|                                   <@SECONDARY@>e|export session
@sess|Main/StemExport|                        <@SECONDARY@><@TERTIARY@>e|stem export

; Import audio (Cubase: Cmd+Shift+I equivalent)
@sess|Common/addExistingAudioFiles|                         <@PRIMARY@>i|import audio files

; Open recent (Cubase: no default, but useful)
@sess|Main/Recent|                              <@PRIMARY@><@TERTIARY@>o|open recent session

; Add Track (Cubase: Cmd+Shift+A for audio, Cmd+Shift+I for instrument)
@sess|Main/AddTrackBus|                         <@PRIMARY@><@TERTIARY@>n|add track(s) or bus(ses)


;; =============================================================
;; TRACK OPERATIONS (Cubase-style)
;; =============================================================

; Mute selected track (Cubase: M on channel)
; (m is already used for region mute above)

; Solo selected track (Cubase: S on channel)
@edtrk|Editor/track-solo-toggle|                          <@SECONDARY@>s|toggle track solo status

; Record enable
@edtrk|Editor/track-record-enable-toggle|                  <@TERTIARY@>b|toggle track rec-enable

; MIDI input toggle
@edtrk|Editor/toggle-midi-input-active|                   <@SECONDARY@>i|toggle selected track MIDI input

; Move selected tracks
@vis|Editor/move-selected-tracks-up|                       <@PRIMARY@>Up|move selected tracks up
@vis|Editor/move-selected-tracks-down|                   <@PRIMARY@>Down|move selected tracks down

; Select prev/next strip
@select|Editor/select-prev-stripable|        <@SECONDARY@><@TERTIARY@>Up|select previous strip
@select|Editor/select-next-stripable|      <@SECONDARY@><@TERTIARY@>Down|select next strip


;; =============================================================
;; REGION OPERATIONS
;; =============================================================

@rop|Region/naturalize-region|             <@SECONDARY@>2|move to original position
@rop|Region/normalize-region|              <@SECONDARY@>3|normalize
@rop|Region/reverse-region|                <@SECONDARY@>4|reverse
@rop|Region/quantize-region|               <@SECONDARY@>5|quantize MIDI notes in region
@rop|Region/boost-region-gain|             <@SECONDARY@>6|increase region gain
@rop|Region/cut-region-gain|               <@SECONDARY@>7|reduce region gain
@rop|Region/pitch-shift-region|            <@SECONDARY@>8|transpose
@rop|Region/rename-region|                 <@SECONDARY@>9|rename region
@rop|Region/toggle-opaque-region|          <@SECONDARY@>0|toggle region opacity
@rop|Region/set-fade-in-length|                              <@PRIMARY@>slash|set fade in length
@rop|Region/set-fade-out-length|                         <@PRIMARY@>backslash|set fade out length
@rop|Region/trim-to-previous-region|                       <@PRIMARY@>j|trim region to end of prev region
@rop|Region/trim-to-next-region|                           <@PRIMARY@>k|trim region to start of next region
@rop|Region/export-region|                     <@PRIMARY@><@SECONDARY@>e|export selected region(s)
@rop|Region/show-rhythm-ferret|                           <@SECONDARY@>f|show rhythm ferret window

; Trim operations
@eep|Region/trim-front|                           <@SECONDARY@>bracketleft|trim front
@eep|Region/trim-back|                          <@SECONDARY@>bracketright|trim back
@eep|Region/insert-region-from-source-list|                            i|insert from region list

; Region sync point
@rop|Region/set-region-sync-position|                                  v|set region sync point
@rop|Region/add-region-cue-marker|                       <@TERTIARY@>m|add a region/cue marker

; Align operations
@aep|Region/align-regions-end|                            <@SECONDARY@>a|align end(s)
@aep|Region/align-regions-sync|                            <@TERTIARY@>a|align sync points
@aep|Region/align-regions-start|               <@PRIMARY@><@SECONDARY@>a|align start(s)
@aep|Region/align-regions-start-relative|       <@PRIMARY@><@TERTIARY@>a|align start(s) relative
@aep|Region/align-regions-sync-relative|                <@SECONDARY@>x|align sync points (relative)

; Selection operations
@select|Editor/select-all-after-edit-cursor|    <@PRIMARY@><@TERTIARY@>e|select all after edit point
@gselect|Common/select-all-visible-lanes|                   <@PRIMARY@>t|select all visible lanes
@gselect|Common/invert-selection|               <@PRIMARY@><@TERTIARY@>i|invert selection
@select|Editor/select-all-between-cursors|                  <@PRIMARY@>u|select all enclosed by range
@select|Editor/select-all-in-punch-range|                  <@TERTIARY@>d|select all in punch range

; Edit point cycling
@eep|Editor/cycle-edit-point|                  <@TERTIARY@>2|next edit point (playhead, mouse)
@eep|Editor/cycle-edit-point-with-marker|      <@PRIMARY@>2|next edit point with marker
@eep|Editor/edit-cursor-to-previous-region-sync|           apostrophe|EP to prev region sync
@eep|Editor/edit-cursor-to-next-region-sync|                semicolon|EP to next region sync

; Play selected regions
@edit|Region/play-selected-regions|                       <@SECONDARY@>h|play selected region(s)

; Loop/Punch ranges
@ranges|Editor/set-loop-from-edit-range|                   bracketright|set loop range from edit range
@ranges|Editor/set-punch-from-edit-range|                   bracketleft|set punch range from edit range


;; =============================================================
;; GRID / SNAP (Cubase-style)
;; =============================================================

; Cycle snap mode (Cubase: J)
; (j already mapped above)

; Grid unit cycling
@grid|Editing/prev-grid-choice|                          <@TERTIARY@>j|use prev grid unit
@grid|Editing/next-grid-choice|              <@PRIMARY@><@TERTIARY@>j|use next grid unit


;; =============================================================
;; NUMPAD TRANSPORT (Cubase-style)
;; =============================================================

; Numpad * = Record (Cubase standard)
; Numpad / = Cycle on/off (Cubase standard)
; Numpad 0 = Stop (Cubase standard)
; Numpad 1 = Go to Left Locator (Cubase standard)
; Numpad 2 = Go to Right Locator (Cubase standard)
; Numpad . = Go to project start (Cubase standard)

@numpad|Transport/numpad-decimal|                              KP_Decimal|go to project start
@numpad|Transport/alternate-numpad-decimal|                  KP_Separator|go to project start (alternate)
@numpad|Transport/numpad-0|KP_0|stop
@numpad|Transport/numpad-1|KP_1|go to left locator
@numpad|Transport/numpad-2|KP_2|go to right locator
@numpad|Transport/numpad-3|KP_3|to marker 3
@numpad|Transport/numpad-4|KP_4|to marker 4
@numpad|Transport/numpad-5|KP_5|to marker 5
@numpad|Transport/numpad-6|KP_6|to marker 6
@numpad|Transport/numpad-7|KP_7|to marker 7
@numpad|Transport/numpad-8|KP_8|to marker 8
@numpad|Transport/numpad-9|KP_9|to marker 9

@gmark|Common/alternate-add-location-from-playhead|              KP_Enter|add marker at playhead
@gmark|Common/alternate-remove-location-from-playhead|<@PRIMARY@>KP_Enter|remove marker at playhead
@gmark|Common/alternate-jump-forward-to-mark|   <@PRIMARY@>KP_Right|to next mark
@gmark|Common/alternate-jump-backward-to-mark|   <@PRIMARY@>KP_Left|to previous mark

@select|Editor/nudge-backward|                   KP_Subtract|nudge backward
@trans|Common/nudge-next-backward|    <@PRIMARY@>KP_Subtract|nudge next backward
@select|Editor/nudge-forward|                   KP_Add|nudge forward
@trans|Common/nudge-next-forward|    <@PRIMARY@>KP_Add|nudge next forward


;; =============================================================
;; GLOBAL EDITING OPERATIONS
;; =============================================================

@gedt|Common/start-range|                        comma|set start of range
